canvas 1
collection @gatekeeper-build-plan "Gatekeeper build — removals, done, tasks" {

  node @rm-table concept "Removed capabilities — second version, corrected against the audit" role=warning size=large {
    table @rm-t columns=["Removed", "Affects", "What it does today", "Plain words — what changes for you", "Risk to weigh"] {
      row @rm-r1 cells=["G0 · Edit lock (three places: workspace-session.ts:1064-1072, canvas/core/interaction/changes.ts:22, submission-session.ts:60)", "Your screen (all diagrams)", "While an earlier edit, undo or review is still being processed, the app refuses any new edit. The lock exists in three separate places, not one.", "If you click or drag twice quickly, the second edit is currently dropped. After the change, both edits go to the server.", "Without the lock, the second edit arrives on a stale base and the server answers revision-conflict. Turn-taking and rebase rules (stage 2) must exist FIRST, or fast editing gets worse, not better."]
      row @rm-r2 cells=["G1 · Movement review (the modules-only review interrupt)", "Your screen (module diagrams only)", "When you drag a node in a module diagram, the app can interrupt with a review offering two kinds of options: rearrange the section, or expand the group. The first version of this table called it only a rearrange popup — that was wrong.", "The review interrupt dies, and with it the rearrange shortcut. The EXPAND half survives — it already grows groups today and becomes the 'keep in' answer in the new popup. This is a screen change, not an agent-authoring change.", "The rearrange shortcut has no replacement in this plan — confirm you do not rely on it. The teardown is the biggest deletion in the build (~2,100 lines across the review machinery)."]
      row @rm-r3 cells=["G2 · Planner hard-fail ('captured group missing')", "Your screen (mostly module diagrams)", "Groups and trees can be collapsed so their children are hidden (folding). A drag touching collapsed or absent content can stop with the error 'captured group missing'; the server is never asked, so nothing is saved. On the placement path this is already caught as stale-target.", "A drag that fails with that error today will instead reach the server and either work or get a clear refusal.", "More cases now reach the server. Until the server has answers for them, you may see refusals where you previously saw a failed drag with a technical message — so the refusals must be readable (stage 9)."]
      row @rm-r4 cells=["G3 · Browser roads engine (route-preview.ts)", "Your screen (module diagrams)", "Module diagrams draw wires between modules along planned routes (roads). Today your browser re-computes these routes itself before the server is asked.", "Roads still draw exactly as today, and the visibility toggle still works — only who computes them changes. Your browser stops calculating and asks the server's existing preview instead. If the server cannot be reached, you see 'judge unreachable'.", "Previews are full server renders, so they may appear later than today's local solve — this is unmeasured, and a drop that previews then commits pays two renders. This is the change called 'the gatekeeper becomes a messenger'."]
      row @rm-r5 cells=["G4 · Journal wedge — ALREADY HALF FIXED (submission-session.ts)", "Your screen", "The app records each edit it sends. A plainly refused edit already frees the next edit (PR #104). What still blocks everything is an edit with an UNCERTAIN fate — the request may or may not have saved (transport failure).", "An edit whose fate is uncertain can be reconciled (the app finds out what happened), and then you keep working. Today that wedge is permanent.", "Reconciling must look up what actually happened before releasing — releasing blindly risks applying the same edit twice. The existing reconcile/retry functions are the base."]
      row @rm-r6 cells=["The browser as a decider (all five above)", "Your screen", "Five checks inside your browser decide what is allowed before the server is asked. For a human edit, the browser's answer is final today — the server may never see the edit.", "Your browser presents and the server decides. Humans and agents are answered by the same place — and that place largely exists today (admission, planner, feasibility render, atomic commit, plus a preview route humans can already use).", "Every answer now needs a server round-trip, and refusals come from the server. The design accepts this; it is the point of the change."]
    }
    text @rm-note "Corrected against the Opus 5.5 audit: G0 lives in three places, G1 includes the expand half (which survives), G2 is mostly a modules problem, and G4 was already half-fixed by PR #104. Each row is something the app does today that it will stop doing after the build. If a row is unclear or unacceptable, raise it before the build starts." role=caption
  }

  node @done-table concept "Definition of done — exact checks, exact pass conditions" role=primary size=large {
    table @done-t columns=["#", "The exact check", "Execute — command / function", "Pass condition (math)"] {
      row @done-r1 cells=["D1", "On every diagram mode, drag node N out of group G: the drop lands, a popup offers keep-in / move-out / cancel, and choosing move-out commits and survives a reload", "Headless browser per mode; popup = drop-choice.askMeaning(); keep-in = movement-expand.buildExpandOption(); move-out = regroup section replace", "(popup options = {keep-in, move-out, cancel}; after reload parent(N) != G; must hold for all modes m in {flow, tree, er, modules, sequence})"]
      row @done-r2 cells=["D2", "Send the same SEMANTIC edit at the same base revision R once as a browser drag and once as DSL text (an equivalent edit — the identical request is impossible: actor must match the caller and agents cannot use the model planner)", "Browser drag -> admit -> prepare(preview=true); CLI: pnpm canvas preview FILE --revision R; if committing, pnpm canvas apply REQUEST_ID", "(verdict_browser(R) = verdict_CLI(R); if both commit, new_revision_browser = new_revision_CLI)"]
      row @done-r3 cells=["D3", "No browser code decides LEGALITY before the server is asked. Transport guards may remain (one edit in flight, stale-gesture) but their answer is 'wait / retry', never a legality verdict", "grep for legality refusals on the apps/web drag path; live drag with the server stopped", "(legality verdicts issued in apps/web = 0; stopped server -> message = 'judge unreachable' and local verdicts = 0)"]
      row @done-r4 cells=["D4", "An edit left UNCERTAIN by a transport failure can be reconciled, and the next edit then commits", "Force an uncertain entry, reconcile via submission-session.reconcile()/retry(), then commit a valid edit E2", "(journal(E1).state = uncertain -> reconciled to a known fate; outcome(E2) = committed; no edit applied twice)"]
      row @done-r5 cells=["D5", "Every refusal is plain words plus options; no raw codes on any user-visible surface", "Trigger each refusal type (rule broken, not drawable, revision conflict, judge unreachable) -> diagnostics.toHumanWords() (extends the PR #104 mapping)", "(raw codes shown = 0; options shown = {retry, adjust, cancel} for every refusal type)"]
      row @done-r6 cells=["D6", "Module diagrams have no modules-only review interrupt and no browser roads engine; one law set serves all modes", "grep for modules-only branches on the drag path; run D1 on a modules diagram", "(modules-only drag-path branches = 0; D1(modules) = pass)"]
      row @done-r7 cells=["D7", "pnpm check shows no new failures versus main", "Run pnpm check on the branch; diff the failures against the recorded main baseline", "(new failures on branch = 0)"]
      row @done-r8 cells=["D8", "The known broken module-node drag on main (PR #106's target) is fixed or explicitly deferred in writing", "Headless drag of a module node, or append the written decision to this collection", "(node position after commit = drop position) or (written deferral exists in this collection)"]
    }
    text @done-note "These are gates, unlike the line estimates. If a row cannot be proven, the build is not done. D2 and D4 were rewritten after the audit: D2 was impossible as first written, and D4 described a problem PR #104 already fixed." role=caption
  }

  node @task-table concept "Task list — the stage tracker (read top to bottom = build order)" role=primary size=large {
    table @task-t columns=["Stage", "Task", "What the builder is doing", "Task done when…", "Est. lines (+/-)", "What you will observe", "Achieves"] {
      row @task-r1 cells=["1 of 10", "Reconcile uncertain submissions", "submission-session.ts + records/submission.ts + submissions.ts: an edit whose fate is uncertain (transport failure) gets a reconcile path that finds out what happened before freeing the diagram", "An uncertain entry reconciles, then a valid edit commits (D4)", "+60 / -15", "A diagram stuck after a failed save can be unstuck without losing work.", "D4"]
      row @task-r2 cells=["2 of 10", "Turn-taking: rebase rules", "admission.ts + authoring api.ts + feasibility.ts: a revision-conflict answer says what changed and how to rebase, instead of a bare conflict", "A second quick edit gets a rebase answer, not a dead end", "+50 / -5", "Nothing yet. This exists so stage 8 does not make fast editing worse.", "enables D3"]
      row @task-r3 cells=["3 of 10", "The group-edge popup", "drop-choice.ts (new, drafts) + drafts/regroup.ts + CanvasSurface.tsx: the drop lands, then keep-in / move-out / cancel at the drop spot", "The popup works on every diagram mode", "+210 / -10", "Drop a node on a group's edge and a popup asks: keep in group, move out, or cancel.", "D1"]
      row @task-r4 cells=["4 of 10", "Capture and plan both meanings", "movement-capture.ts stops throwing; plan.ts + regroup.ts + movement.ts turn one ambiguous drop into two candidate requests (keep-in, move-out)", "A group-edge drop yields both plans; nothing throws", "+195 / -95", "Drags that used to stop with 'captured group missing' now work or get a clear refusal.", "D1, D3"]
      row @task-r5 cells=["5 of 10", "Keep-in rewired to expand", "movement-expand.ts: buildExpandOption() (which already grows groups today) is rewired from the review to the popup", "Choosing keep-in grows the group and persists after reload", "+60 / -40", "'keep in' grows the group around the node. This reuses existing code, not new machinery.", "D1"]
      row @task-r6 cells=["6 of 10", "Route-preview asks the server", "route-preview.ts: the in-browser roads solve is deleted; previews call the existing server preview route", "No roads engine in the browser; browser and CLI share one pipeline (D2)", "+30 / -70", "Wire previews on module diagrams may appear later; they match what the server will commit.", "D2, D3, D6"]
      row @task-r7 cells=["7 of 10", "Movement-review teardown", "movement-rearrange.ts, movement-preview.ts, movement-intent.ts, MovementReview.tsx, records/movement.ts, compose.ts: the review machinery is gutted; expand (stage 5) is what survives", "The review interrupt is gone from every drag path", "+55 / -1476", "Module drags stop being interrupted by the review. The rearrange shortcut is gone (removals, row G1).", "D3, D6"]
      row @task-r8 cells=["8 of 10", "Edit locks removed", "workspace-session.ts + interaction/changes.ts: the lock is deleted in all three places (the third, submission-session, went in stage 1)", "No local legality verdict on the drag path (D3); rapid edits get server answers in turn", "+45 / -390", "Rapid successive edits stop being silently dropped. Requires stage 2 first.", "D3"]
      row @task-r9 cells=["9 of 10", "Refusals in human words", "diagnostics.ts: the existing plain-English mapping (PR #104) is extended with the laws' typed reasons", "Every refusal surface passes D5", "+45 / 0", "A refused edit tells you why in plain words and offers retry, adjust, or cancel.", "D5"]
      row @task-r10 cells=["10 of 10", "Modules loses special cases + session split", "Delete the remaining modules-only branches; decide and land (or write down the deferral of) the workspace-session split", "D6 passes; the split lands or its deferral is written down", "included above", "Module diagrams behave like every other diagram. No module-only popups.", "D6"]
    }
    text @task-note "During the build, 'stage 4 of 10' refers to this table. Line estimates sum exactly to B.4's second-count totals (+750 / -2101); stage 10 is the removal half of earlier stages plus a decision, not new work. D7 and D8 are whole-build checks made after stage 10, so no single stage owns them." role=caption
  }

  section @s-removed "1 · Removed capabilities — what changes, and the risk of each (corrected)" mode=flow direction=right order=0 {
    show @rm-table
  }

  section @s-done "2 · Definition of done — exact checks, exact pass conditions" mode=flow direction=right order=1 {
    show @done-table
  }

  section @s-tasks "3 · Task list — ten stages, tracked here" mode=flow direction=right order=2 {
    show @task-table
  }
}
